<title>NETHERLANDS: BOSKALIS NET FALLS IN 1996.</title>
<headline>BOSKALIS NET FALLS IN 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PAPENDRECHT, Netherlands 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)	     2.42 vs   2.79</p>
<p>    Net profit			    62.1  vs  70.9</p>
<p>    Dividend (guilders)		  1.10 vs   1.10</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had expected Koninklijke Boskalis</p>
<p>Westminster NV, the world's largest dredger, to report a net</p>
<p>profit from ordinary operations of between 62 million and 72</p>
<p>million guilders.</p>
<p>    Turnover (billions)		  1.26 vs   1.09</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    62.9  vs  68.0</p>
<p>    Interest gains			 2.6  vs   6.6</p>
<p>    Associates' income		   7.6  vs   6.4</p>
<p>    Tax				     11.0  vs  10.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Boskalis said the 1996 dividend could be taken up</p>
<p>either fully in cash or as an optional 0.60 guilders in cash</p>
<p>plus a payment in new shares. Details of the optional cash plus</p>
<p>stock dividend will be published on May 23.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
